"view.enneagramscreen.help"           = "Through the Enneagram screen, you calculate the relative values of the nine Enneagram personality types. The calculation is based on an idea by Dutch researcher Sjoerd Visser.\n\nOverview tab\nThe Overview tab shows an Enneagram figure and a table of results. In the figure, each type is represented by a numbered circle: the strongest type is shown in red, the second and third in orange, and the remaining circles in blue. The table lists all nine types sorted by strength, with the strongest type at the top. Tap any circle or any row in the table to read a description of that type.\n\nOptions panel (right column)\nIn the right panel you can select which planets are included in the calculation. By default all planets are used, as this reflects the original research. You can deselect individual planets to observe their effect on the outcome.\n\nIf you only have a date without a time, you can disable Include houses — Enigma will then omit all calculations related to house positions.\n\nThere are two versions of the Enneagram theory: the original from 2010, and an improved version from 2012. The updated version is selected by default. Uncheck Use updated version to see the results according to the older 2010 tables.\n\nYou can also enable Count Pluto twice. For the reasoning behind this, please refer to the user manual.\n\nNote that the calculation always uses Placidus houses and geocentric positions, as this is how the original research was performed. Any change to the options is applied immediately.\n\nDetails tab\nThe Details tab shows a table with the individual contribution of each planet to each of the nine Enneagram types. This can be useful if you wish to study how the calculation works.";

